check=first-pass-issues-the-authored-argv
operator=guard-deletion
target=src/Amoebius/Host/Ensure.hs
mutation=replace | src/Amoebius/Host/Ensure.hs | installAndVerify reresolve installer plan config requested = case lookupTool requested config of\n  Just _ -> pure (Right config)\n  Nothing -> drive plan config | installAndVerify reresolve installer plan config requested = pure (Right config)
statement=Report converged from the config the run was handed, without probing for the requested
statement=tool at all. The driver returns success on a host where nothing is installed, and the
statement=absent arm is never reached -- so the run issues no install argv whatsoever. It still
statement="converges", which is exactly why convergence alone cannot be the check: the evidence is
statement=the recorded argv set, not a return code.
